    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nDNG McKenna Healy are delighted to present No. 49 Ballygossan Park, a wonderful three-bedroom mid-terrace home brought to the market in pristine condition throughout.\n\nDesigned with modern living in mind, this impressive B-rated property offers bright, spacious and energy-efficient accommodation, enhanced by extra-high ceilings on the ground floor and triple-glazed windows. Further features include a ground-floor double bedroom, a main bedroom with en-suite, a guest WC and a beautifully landscaped private rear garden.\n\nAn inviting entrance hallway leads to a spacious and comfortable living room. To the rear is a bright and airy kitchen/dining room, where French doors open directly onto the landscaped garden, creating a seamless connection between the indoor and outdoor living spaces. A generous double bedroom and guest WC complete the ground-floor accommodation. The flexible bedroom arrangement makes the home particularly suitable for guests, older children, those working from home or anyone seeking accessible ground-floor accommodation.\n\nUpstairs, there are two further double bedrooms, including a spacious main bedroom with en-suite, together with a stylish family bathroom.\n\nOutside, the property benefits from a large, private landscaped rear garden, providing an ideal setting for outdoor dining, entertaining and family life. To the front, there is off-street parking together with a designated bin-storage area.\n\nBallygossan Park is a highly regarded modern development conveniently located within walking distance of Skerries town centre and its excellent selection of schools, shops, cafés, restaurants, bars and beautiful sandy beaches. Skerries Train Station is approximately a 12-minute walk away, while regular rail and bus services provide convenient access to Dublin City Centre.\n\nAn excellent range of sporting and recreational facilities is also available locally, including sailing, golf, rugby, GAA and tennis clubs.\n\nSkerries is a thriving coastal town renowned for its wonderful beaches, picturesque harbour and vibrant community atmosphere. Dublin Airport and the M1 motorway are approximately 12 miles away, making No. 49 an ideal choice for those seeking a beautifully presented, energy-efficient home within easy commuting distance of Dublin City Centre."
      },
